From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:40:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Compile the Windows resources natively too

lmms.exe and RemoteZynAddSubFx.exe compile their .rc files with
${WINDRES}, which only the MinGW cross-compile toolchain files set. A
native MSYS2 build leaves it empty, and the build fails to run "".
Fall back to the resource compiler CMake found.

Upstream: not submitted
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index d9bc44e..72a503a 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -523,6 +523,11 @@ IF(GIT_FOUND AND NOT CONTRIBUTORS)
 		TIMEOUT 1)
 ENDIF()
 
+# the cross toolchain files name windres; native builds use CMake's
+IF(WIN32 AND NOT WINDRES)
+	SET(WINDRES "${CMAKE_RC_COMPILER}")
+ENDIF()
+
 # embedded resources stuff
 IF(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
 	# compile buildtools native
